 "x-high-extensions": [
  "book: id pattern <subject>_<9-12>, grade 9-12, subjects of the High (Grade 9-12) textbooks.",
  "book.intro (optional, list of strings): header lines of the source notes shown before Unit 1 (title, motto, how-to-study).",
  "book.intro_cards (optional, list of cards): notes that belong to the whole book, not to one unit (how these notes work, exam technique, whole-book study advice). Same card types as lessons.",
  "book.source_outline (list of {level, text}): the heading outline of the source HTML notes, in order (traceability; the app may ignore it).",
  "card.id (required in High): unique id \"<unit id>-cNN\" (intro cards: \"<abbr><grade>-intro-cNN\"); unitMap nodes and index.json topics link to these ids.",
  "card.src / game.src / glossary.src / tip.src / question.src (optional): where the item comes from: \"notes\" (the source HTML notes), \"glossary\" (built from the unit glossary), or \"textbook p.N\" / \"textbook pp.N–M\" (enrichment from the official textbook, printed page).",
  "enriched: true (optional, on cards, glossary items, tips, exercise questions): item added from the textbook, not in the source notes.",
  "card.style (optional): \"timeline\" (table card built from a timeline) or \"steps\" (numbered procedure). Renderers may ignore it.",
  "table card presentation (all optional; head and rows stay the full table so older app versions still show it): kind = \"table\" (default) | \"journal\" | \"ledger\" | \"statement\" | \"t_account\"; cols = one type per column: \"text\" | \"num\" | \"money\" | \"dr\" | \"cr\" | \"date\" | \"ref\" (guessed from the header and cells when absent; num/money/dr/cr are right-aligned, money/dr/cr regrouped with thousands separators); marks = one per row: \"\" | \"head\" (section heading, or a new account in a t_account card) | \"total\" (single rule above the figures) | \"final\" (rule above, double rule below) | \"note\" (narration, italic) | \"indent\" | \"bold\"; frozen = number of leading columns kept in view while a wide table scrolls sideways; layout (how narrow screens show it) = \"grid\" | \"cards\" (one coloured card per row) | \"stack\" (cards on every width) | \"compare\" (one coloured card per compared column) | \"terms\" (two-line term / explanation list) | \"proscons\" (green advantages / red disadvantages sections; points separated by \"; \") | \"sections\" (accounting: toggle between the column groups named before \" — \" in the headers) | \"entries\" (accounting: one block per row with labelled Dr / Cr figure chips); key_point = one sentence shown under the table in a \"Remember this!\" box; to = prefix for journal credit lines (e.g. \"To \"). A t_account card's rows are a head row [account, number, ...] followed by [particulars, amount, particulars, amount] (or [date, particulars, amount, date, particulars, amount]) lines: Dr on the left, Cr on the right.",
  "card.reveal (optional, reading/worked cards): the label of the source reveal button (\"Suggested answers\", \"Show steps\").",
  "card.from_global (optional): the card was split out of an end-of-book review section (sticky wall, formula wall, revision checklist) and placed in the unit it belongs to.",
  "tip.card (optional): id of the card this memory tip repeats.",
  "unit.unitMap (required in High): concept map of the unit, see $defs/unitMap.",
  "unit.note (optional): editorial note about the unit (e.g. textbook pages missing from the PDF).",
  "exercise.questions: no maxItems in High (source units carry 20-40 quiz items; all are kept); minItems stays 8.",
  "question.src \"exam\" + question.exam_question: a matric/model exam question (examprep content, answer + explanation steps copied) used to bring a thin unit to 8 exercise questions.",
  "question.section (optional): source heading the quiz item came from. question.label (optional): source numbering (e.g. \"Q12 · bio — ...\").",
  "question.orig (optional): on an enriched textbook true/false item whose answer is false, the true textbook sentence (the statement was made false by changing one year to another year from the same unit); the explanation quotes it.",
  "question.answer_src / question.why_src (optional): where the model answer / explanation was taken from, for open prompts that had no answer in the source (\"textbook p.N\" or \"notes card <id>\").",
  "question.similar[].exam_question (optional): id of the matric/model exam question (examprep content) used as the similar question.",
  "game.from_card (optional): card id a sort game was built from.",
  "Diagram SVGs live in content/notes/svg/<book id>/ (clean standalone SVG: viewBox kept, CSS variables and class styles inlined, no scripts)."
 ]
}
